# Context First

Before planning or implementing any change, read the relevant files under `.specs/codebase/` and `.specs/project/`:

| Change type | Read |
| ----- | ----- |
| General code | `CONVENTIONS.md`, `STRUCTURE.md` |
| Scanner modules (git, complexity, scoring, scan-result, config, report) | `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CONCERNS.md`, `INTEGRATIONS.md` |
| Progress / milestones | `ROADMAP.md`, `STATE.md`, `.specs/features/` |
| Tests | `TESTING.md` |
| Architecture / stack | `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `STACK.md` |
| External integrations | `INTEGRATIONS.md` |
| Fragile areas | `CONCERNS.md` |
| JSON contract | `schemas/`, `TESTING.md` § contract |

## Living documentation

Every significant change (new scanner modules, domain types, CLI flags) must be reflected in the corresponding `.specs/codebase/` files. Feature complete → update [ROADMAP.md](../../.specs/project/ROADMAP.md) per [roadmap-sync.md](../skills/vitals-spec-driven/references/roadmap-sync.md).

**Where content goes:** milestone history and Execute status → `ROADMAP.md` / `STATE.md` / `.specs/features/`; present-tense design (modules, pipelines, contracts, constraints) → [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../.specs/codebase/ARCHITECTURE.md); present-tense fragile risks → [CONCERNS.md](../../.specs/codebase/CONCERNS.md); present-tense coding conventions → [CONVENTIONS.md](../../.specs/codebase/CONVENTIONS.md); present-tense external adapters (spawn/deps/fs ownership) → [INTEGRATIONS.md](../../.specs/codebase/INTEGRATIONS.md); present-tense stack / deps / publish inventory → [STACK.md](../../.specs/codebase/STACK.md). When editing ARCHITECTURE, follow [architecture-sot.mdc](architecture-sot.mdc) (no `M##` / `HOTSPOT-*` changelog voice). When editing CONCERNS, follow [concerns-sot.mdc](concerns-sot.mdc) (same ban on milestone/changelog voice). When editing CONVENTIONS, follow [conventions-sot.mdc](conventions-sot.mdc) (no `M##` changelog voice; `HOTSPOT-*` naming prefix allowed). When editing INTEGRATIONS, follow [integrations-sot.mdc](integrations-sot.mdc) (same ban on milestone/changelog voice). When editing STACK, follow [stack-sot.mdc](stack-sot.mdc) (same ban on milestone/changelog voice).

